# Complete List of Useful Display Nodes for a Qt/C++ Node Editor

Organized by category so the editor feels consistent and complete.

---

# Basic Value Displays

## 1. Number Display ✅

Shows:

* int
* float
* double

Examples:

```text
42
3.1415
0.98
```

---

## 2. Text Display ✅

Shows:

* strings
* logs
* debug output
* JSON

---

## 3. Boolean Indicator ✅

Visual ON/OFF state.

Examples:

* LED indicator
* colored circle
* checkbox

---

## 4. Vector Display ✅

Shows:

```text
X: 1.2
Y: 5.4
Z: 8.1
```

Useful for:

* 2D/3D math
* physics
* transforms

---

# Image & Graphics Displays

## 5. Image Preview ✅

Displays:

* QImage
* textures
* OpenCV frames

---

## 6. Video Preview ✅

Displays:

* webcam
* video streams
* rendered animation

---

## 7. Texture Preview ❌ (needs OpenGL)

For:

* GPU textures
* shaders
* materials

---

## 8. Thumbnail Grid ❌

Shows multiple images/assets.

Useful for:

* datasets
* texture atlases
* galleries

---

## 9. Sprite Preview ❌ (needs Qt3D)

2D game sprites.

---

## 10. Framebuffer Preview ❌ (needs OpenGL)

Displays rendering pipeline outputs.

---

# Signal / Audio Displays

## 11. Waveform Viewer ❌ (needs realtime audio)

Shows:

* sine waves
* audio samples
* signal data

Equation:

y(t)=A\sin(2\pi f t+\phi)

---

## 12. FFT Spectrum ❌ (needs FFT library)

Frequency-domain visualization.

---

## 13. Spectrogram ❌ (needs FFT library)

Time-frequency heatmap.

Useful for:

* audio analysis
* DSP

---

## 14. Oscilloscope ❌ (needs realtime audio)

Realtime waveform monitor.

---

## 15. VU Meter ❌ (needs audio)

Audio loudness meter.

---

## 16. Stereo Balance Meter ❌ (needs audio)

Left/right channel visualization.

---

