# Recommended "Core Pack"

If you want a sensible first release, start with:

| Priority  | Node            |
| --------- | --------------- |
| Essential | Number Display  |
| Essential | Text Display    |
| Essential | Image Preview   |
| Essential | Plot Graph      |
| Essential | Waveform Viewer |
| Essential | Video Preview   |
| Essential | Console Output  |
| Essential | Table View      |
| Advanced  | FFT Spectrum    |
| Advanced  | Heatmap         |
| Advanced  | 3D Preview      |
| Advanced  | Shader Output   |

That already feels like a real professional node editor package.

A concise professional description you can use for your node/package:

---

## LED Matrix Display Node ✅ (`output/display/ledMatrix`)

A realtime LED matrix display node designed for rendering static text and numeric values in a classic pixel-matrix style. The node accurately displays incoming data using configurable matrix dimensions, allowing the display size to be adjusted dynamically through node properties.

The display updates continuously at millisecond intervals, ensuring the rendered output always reflects the latest incoming value without requiring scrolling or animation. Ideal for dashboards, embedded simulations, retro displays, debugging interfaces, signal visualization, and realtime monitoring systems.

### Features

* Realtime millisecond updates
* Static non-scrolling display
* Accurate text and numeric rendering
* Dynamic matrix width and height
* Adjustable LED pixel size and spacing
* Supports custom foreground/background colors
* Lightweight and efficient rendering
* Designed for Qt/C++ node-based systems

### Supported Inputs

* Integer values
* Floating-point values
* Strings/text
* Boolean states
* Formatted data streams

### Common Use Cases

* Digital counters
* Status panels
* Telemetry displays
* Industrial dashboards
* Retro LED simulations
* Embedded UI visualization
* Debug and monitoring tools

### Properties

* Matrix Width
* Matrix Height
* LED Size
* Pixel Spacing
* Text Color
* Background Color
* Refresh Interval (ms)
* Font/Character Set
* Brightness Intensity

### Behavior

The node renders incoming values as a static LED matrix representation. Whenever the input changes, the display refreshes immediately while maintaining stable non-scrolling output behavior.


